2026-09-27T07:42:45.0523814Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0524000Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0524272Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0524537Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0524639Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0524837Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0524947Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0525097Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0525464Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0525675Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0525785Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0526046Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0526210Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0526341Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0526728Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0527066Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0527707Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0528214Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0528317Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0528723Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0529241Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0529513Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0529796Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0530181Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0530783Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0531096Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0531279Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0533465Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0535808Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0536181Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0603937Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0605272Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0606378Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0607529Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0608228Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0608950Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0609106Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0609486Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0609715Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0611910Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0613944Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0615109Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0616662Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:45.0617035Z 
